    {
      "id": "discussion:10:speech:1",
      "seq": 1,
      "speaker": "arwyn",
      "text": "I'd attend a short shared reading if the selections were brief enough to discuss properly. What makes it welcoming? Knowing the time limit in advance, and that silence between readings is allowed.",
      "at": {
        "day": 1,
        "minute": 420
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "discussion:10:speech:2",
      "seq": 2,
      "speaker": "arwyn",
      "text": "I've found that a clear ending time matters more than the starting one. If people know they can leave after thirty minutes without apology, they show up. And a facilitator who's comfortable with silence — who doesn't rush to fill it — changes what gets said.",
      "at": {
        "day": 1,
        "minute": 420
      }
    }
